to a non-autonomous obstacle problem, formulated as
 \begin{equation*}
 \min\left\{\frac1p\int_\omega |u|^{p} \, dx, \, \text{div}\,a(x,u,\nabla u), \, \varphi \right\}, 
 \end{equation*}
 within a bounded domain $\omega \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ with $n\geq 2$. The structure of $a$ is specified in detail in the assumptions, and the underlying problem is supplemented with suitable boundary conditions. Given the parameter $s$, representing the regularity of the obstacle, we determine the enhanced differentiability of the solution, subject to standard growth, continuity, and convexity conditions applicable to the operator $a$.
